Microsoft Learn: Host Your Domain on Azure DNS

Platform: Microsoft Learn
Module: Host Your Domain on Azure DNS
Track: AZ-104 Microsoft Azure Administrator
Difficulty: Intermediate
Date: 2026

Objective

Learn how to use Azure DNS to host domain names, create and manage DNS zones, configure DNS records, and implement alias records for dynamic name resolution.

This module focused on deploying Azure DNS zones, managing DNS records, mapping domain names to Azure resources, and simplifying DNS management through Azure-integrated alias records.

Step 1: Understanding Azure DNS

The module introduced Azure DNS as Microsoft's cloud-based Domain Name System (DNS) hosting service.

DNS translates human-friendly domain names into IP addresses that computers use to communicate.

Example:
www.contoso.com
       ↓
20.45.100.10

Without DNS, users would need to remember IP addresses instead of website names.

Benefits of Azure DNS:
Global availability
High performance
High reliability
Azure integration
Centralized management
Role-based access control (RBAC)

The module emphasized that Azure DNS hosts DNS records but does not host websites themselves.

Step 2: Understanding DNS Zones

The training introduced DNS zones as containers for DNS records.

A DNS zone represents a domain and stores DNS records associated with that domain.

Example:
contoso.com
DNS Zone Contains:
contoso.com
├── A Records
├── CNAME Records
├── MX Records
├── TXT Records
└── Alias Records
Key concepts learned:
One DNS zone represents one domain
DNS records are stored inside DNS zones
Azure DNS manages public DNS records for internet name resolution

The module demonstrated how DNS zones organize domain information.

Step 3: Configuring Azure DNS to Host a Domain

A major focus of the module was configuring Azure DNS for domain hosting.

Deployment process:
Create DNS Zone
Create DNS Records
Update domain registrar nameservers
Verify DNS resolution
Example:
Domain:
contoso.com

DNS Zone:
contoso.com

Nameservers:
ns1-01.azure-dns.com
ns2-01.azure-dns.net
Key lessons learned:
Azure DNS becomes authoritative for the domain
Registrar nameservers must point to Azure DNS
