The module emphasized understanding authoritative DNS hosting.

Step 4: Understanding DNS Record Types

The training covered common DNS record types.

A Record

Maps a hostname directly to an IPv4 address.

Example:

www.contoso.com
      ↓
20.45.100.10
CNAME Record

Creates an alias to another DNS name.

Example:

blog.contoso.com
      ↓
contoso.azurewebsites.net
MX Record

Defines mail server destinations.

Example:

contoso.com
      ↓
mail.contoso.com
TXT Record

Stores verification and configuration information.

Common uses:

Domain verification
SPF records
Security validation

The module highlighted A records as one of the most commonly used record types.

