Step 7: Understanding Alias Records

A major focus of the module was Azure DNS Alias Records.

Alias records provide dynamic DNS resolution for Azure resources.

Supported Azure resources:
Public IP Addresses
Azure Traffic Manager
Azure Front Door
Azure CDN endpoints
Benefits:
Automatic updates
Reduced maintenance
Simplified DNS management
Example:

Traditional A Record:

www.contoso.com
      ↓
20.45.100.10

If the IP changes:

DNS must be updated manually

Alias Record:

www.contoso.com
      ↓
Azure Resource

If the IP changes:

Azure updates automatically

The module emphasized alias records as a modern Azure DNS management feature.

